{"html":"<p>You have circles and rectangles, and you want the total area. Or dogs and cats that each make their own sound. Interfaces, inheritance and polymorphism let one piece of code work with many kinds of objects, each doing the right thing.</p>\n<h2 id=\"interfaces-a-contract\">Interfaces: A Contract</h2>\n<p>An <strong>interface</strong> says what an object can do, without saying how:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">interface</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\"> Shape</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    double</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> area</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">();</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Classes promise to fulfill it with <code>implements</code>:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">record</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\"> Circle</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">double</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> radius) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">implements</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> Shape</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    public</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> double</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> area</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">() {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">        return</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> Math.PI </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">*</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> radius </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">*</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> radius;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">record</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\"> Rectangle</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">double</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> width, </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">double</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> height) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">implements</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> Shape</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    public</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> double</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> area</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">() {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">        return</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> width </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">*</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> height;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Now code can work with any <code>Shape</code>, without knowing which kind:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">List</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">Shape</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">> </span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">shapes</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> List.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">of</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">new</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> Circle</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">1</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">), </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">new</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> Rectangle</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">2</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">3</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">));</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">double</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> total</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 0</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">for</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (Shape</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> shape</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> :</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> shapes) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    total </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">+=</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> shape.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">area</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">();   </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// 3.14… + 6</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>A class can implement <strong>several</strong> interfaces, like <code>Comparable</code> and <code>Serializable</code> at once.</p>\n<h3 id=\"default-methods\">Default Methods</h3>\n<p>An interface can give a method a body with <code>default</code>. Every implementing class gets it, and can override it:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">interface</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\"> Shape</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    double</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> area</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">();</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    default</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> String </span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">describe</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">() {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">        return</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> getClass</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">().</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">getSimpleName</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">() </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">+</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \" of area \"</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> +</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> Math.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">round</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">area</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">());</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p><code>new Rectangle(2, 3).describe()</code> gives <code>Rectangle of area 6</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"inheritance-extends\">Inheritance: extends</h2>\n<p>A class can <strong>extend</strong> one other class and inherit its fields and methods. An <strong>abstract</strong> class can&#39;t be created on its own, and can declare abstract methods that subclasses must write:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">abstract</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> class</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\"> Animal</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    private</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> final</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> String</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> name;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">    Animal</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(String </span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">name</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">        this</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">.name </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> name;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    abstract</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> String </span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">sound</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">();</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    String </span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">speak</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">() {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">        return</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> name </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">+</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \" says \"</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> +</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> sound</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">();</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">class</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\"> Dog</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> extends</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> Animal</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">    Dog</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(String </span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">name</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">        super</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(name);   </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// call Animal's constructor</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    String </span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">sound</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">() {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">        return</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \"woof\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p><code>super(name)</code> runs the parent&#39;s constructor first. <code>new Dog(&quot;Rex&quot;).speak()</code> gives <code>Rex says woof</code>.</p>\n<h3 id=\"overriding\">Overriding</h3>\n<p>A subclass can replace an inherited method. Mark it <code>@Override</code>: the compiler then checks that a matching method really exists, which catches typos. <code>super.method()</code> calls the parent&#39;s version:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">class</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\"> Cat</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> extends</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> Animal</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">    Cat</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(String </span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">name</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">        super</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(name);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    String </span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">sound</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">() {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">        return</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \"meow\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    @</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">Override</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    String </span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">speak</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">() {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">        return</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> super</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">speak</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">() </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">+</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \", then ignores you\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><h2 id=\"polymorphism\">Polymorphism</h2>\n<p><strong>Polymorphism</strong> means &quot;many forms&quot;: a variable of type <code>Animal</code> can hold a <code>Dog</code> or a <code>Cat</code>, and calling a method runs the version of the <strong>real object</strong>, chosen at run time:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">List</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">Animal</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">> </span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">animals</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> List.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">of</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">new</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> Dog</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"Rex\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">), </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">new</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> Cat</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"Tom\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">));</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">for</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (Animal</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> animal</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> :</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> animals) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    System.out.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">println</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(animal.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">speak</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">());</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// Rex says woof</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// Tom says meow, then ignores you</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Even inside <code>Animal.speak()</code>, the call to <code>sound()</code> runs the subclass&#39;s version. This is what lets you add a new kind of animal without changing the loop.</p>\n<h3 id=\"instanceof-patterns\">instanceof Patterns</h3>\n<p>When you really need the specific type, <code>instanceof</code> with a pattern checks and casts in one step:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">if</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (animal </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">instanceof</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> Dog dog) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    System.out.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">println</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"A dog named \"</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> +</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> dog.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">name</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">());</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>If you write this often, it&#39;s usually a sign the behavior should be a method on the class instead.</p>\n<h2 id=\"interface-or-abstract-class\">Interface or Abstract Class?</h2>\n<div data-table-scroll><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Question</th>\n<th>Interface</th>\n<th>Abstract class</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>How many can a class use?</td>\n<td>Many</td>\n<td>One</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Can it hold fields with state?</td>\n<td>No (constants only)</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Can it have constructors?</td>\n<td>No</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Typical use</td>\n<td>A capability: <code>Comparable</code>, <code>Shape</code></td>\n<td>Shared code and state for close relatives</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p>Start with an interface. Use an abstract class when several subclasses truly share fields and code.</p>\n<h2 id=\"composition-over-inheritance\">Composition Over Inheritance</h2>\n<p>Inheritance ties a subclass tightly to its parent: a change in the parent can break every child, and Java allows only one parent. Often it&#39;s better to <strong>have</strong> an object than to <strong>be</strong> one:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// Inheritance: an OrderService IS-A Logger? Not really.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">class</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\"> OrderService</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> extends</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> Logger</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> { … }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// Composition: an OrderService HAS-A Logger. Easy to swap and test.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">class</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\"> OrderService</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    private</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> final</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> Logger</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> logger;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">    OrderService</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(Logger </span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">logger</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">        this</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">.logger </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> logger;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>A good test: use inheritance only when &quot;B is an A&quot; is true in every situation. Otherwise, compose.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-answer-in-short\">The Answer in Short</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>An interface is a contract; a class can implement several, and default methods add shared behavior.</li>\n<li><code>extends</code> inherits from one class; abstract classes hold shared code and leave some methods to subclasses.</li>\n<li>Mark overrides with <code>@Override</code>, and call the parent&#39;s version with <code>super</code>.</li>\n<li>Polymorphism runs the method of the real object, so one loop handles many types.</li>\n<li>Prefer interfaces and composition; inherit only for true &quot;is a&quot; relationships.</li>\n</ol>\n"}